      "seed": 1458043010,
      "version": 66,
      "versionNonce": 964592258,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1785430179763,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "In C++, serialization is the process of converting an object into a sequence of bytes so that it\ncan be stored in memory or transmitted across a network and deserialization is the reverse\nprocess, where the byte stream is used to reconstruct the original object. In this article, we will\nlearn how we can serialize and deserialize an object in C++.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 7,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "In C++, serialization is the process of converting an object into a sequence of bytes so that it can be stored in memory or transmitted across a network and deserialization is the reverse process, where the byte stream is used to reconstruct the original object. In this article, we will learn how we can serialize and deserialize an object in C++.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.15
    },
